// CHECKOUT PROMENADE — HOT CLUB — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// CHECKOUT PROMENADE as Parisian gypsy-jazz swing — a Hot Club quintet in the shop. A game
// alternate of shop, selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk.
// Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Peter: "another where you can do whatever you like. Not a dance mix though."
// 
// At 96 BPM the shop's sixteenths are a swing band's eighths: each half bar is a bar of
// swing at 192, and swing 60 lilts every off-sixteenth. La pompe (a short chord on every
// beat, 2 and 4 accented) is the whole groove — no kit, no kick under the beat. The tune
// is the shop's, note for note (shop.js lead, bars 7–14), with its harmony line and
// twinkle; the chords follow the shop's bass, a chord a beat, as gypsy-jazz changes:
//   A1 | C6 A7 Dm6 G7 |   A2 | C6 Am7 F6 G7 |   B1 | Fmaj7 . Em7 . |   B2 | Am7 . D7 G13 |
// 
//   1–4    intro — the pompe alone on the vamp; bass and the violin's swoop at bar 3;
//          the guitar's pickup run
//   5–8    A — the lead GUITAR has the tune; two-feel bass; no drums
//   9–12   B — the VIOLIN has it an octave up; the guitar answers on the shop's harmony
//          line; brushes in; the bass walks
//   13–16  A — guitar and violin an octave apart; the HARP has the twinkle
//   17–20  A — Charleston stop-time: the band hits and stops, the CLARINET alone on the tune
//   21–24  B — clarinet on the tune, violin on the shop's harmony line
//   25–28  A — the guitar's solo: runs through every gap of the tune, then the tune in octaves
//   29–32  B — the violin's solo over the clarinet's guide tones; A7 on the last beat
//   33–44  SHOUT CHORUS in D — A (guitar, violin an octave up, clarinet harmony), B (guitar
//          octaves, the violin soaring), A (two bars of stop-time, all three on the tune;
//          the last beat a G7 home)
//   45–48  home in C, quietly — the clarinet alone, pompe on 2 and 4, the harp's twinkle
//   49–52  turnaround — the intro again, the violin's swoop, the guitar's pickup into bar 5
// 
// The loop is bars 5–52. Unrendered and unlevelled: lane gains are set by reasoning, and
// the trailing master gain (-4 dB) is an estimate for −21 LUFS.
